PW-1 further deposed that at about 10:00 am, he received an information from GTB Hospital, from his son-in-law Sachin that the condition of his daughter was very serious and called him to the hospital immediately; then PW-1 reached GTB Hospital;
there he found his aforesaid family members present, however, accused was not present there; that he enquired from the doctors about the condition of his daughter Rashmi and he was told by the doctors that the condition of his daughter was serious and it was a Police case as she herself had not banged her head against the wall but some one might have caused injuries on her head; his daughter died on the same day and Police came at the hospital; on the next day, SDM also arrived at the hospital and he made inquiries from PW-1 and recorded his statement Ex.PW1/A; he identified the dead body of his daughter Rashmi vide memo Ex.PW1/B; postmortem on the dead body of his daughter Rashmi was got conducted; that after the postmortem, he received the dead body of his daughter for cremation.
PW-1 further deposed that that under the pressure of accused, Rashmi had taken money from his other daughters Seema, Shilpa and from his wife as well; that the accused was jobless at the time of marriage and after the marriage as well; that at the time of marriage, accused had claimed that he was working with LIC but in fact,

Om Prakash Saini, Section Officer, Health & Family Welfare Department, Government of NCT of Delhi (Exec. Magistrate)- He deposed that on 05.04.2018, he went to Mortuary of GTB Hospital on the request of Police officials of PS Shahdara and as per direction of SDM, Shahdara;
that the family members of the deceased were present there; that he recorded statement of Sh.
Karan Singh (father of deceased) Ex.PW1/A in his handwriting and directed the Police officials to take necessary action as per law.
